---
title: Why Exceptionless?
layout: layouts/base.vto
redirectFrom:
  - /docs/comparison/
description: Why developers choose Exceptionless for error monitoring - open source, self-hostable, predictable pricing, real-time configuration, and an AI assistant that works with your data.
---
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">{{ icons["heart-handshake"] }} Why Exceptionless</p>
    <h1>The bugs you don't know about <span class="text-gradient">cost you users</span></h1>
    <p>Most people who hit an error don't report it. They just leave. Exceptionless shows you what's broken, who it affects, and whether your fix worked, without an enterprise price tag or lock-in.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-sm">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon">{{ icons.users }}</span>
        <h3>Keep the users you worked to win</h3>
        <p>Catch the errors people hit every day but never report, and fix them before frustration turns into churn.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon">{{ icons.rocket }}</span>
        <h3>Spend your time building</h3>
        <p>Stop reproducing bugs from vague reports. Get the stack trace, request, user, and context the first time, then get back to features.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon">{{ icons["badge-check"] }}</span>
        <h3>Be the app that just works</h3>
        <p>Know about regressions before your customers do, and prove that your fixes actually stuck.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {{ include "partials/signup-banner.vto" { cta: "why-top", title: "Find out what your users are running into", secondaryHref: "/tour/", secondaryLabel: "Take the tour" } }}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-subtle">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ icons.star }} What makes us different</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Built by developers, for developers</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Exceptionless has been catching production errors since 2013. Here's what teams tell us made them switch, and stay.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reasons">
      <div class="reason reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon">{{ icons.github }}</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Open source, for real</h3>
          <p>The hosted service runs the same code you can read, audit, and contribute to on GitHub under the Apache 2.0 license. No closed-core features, no surprises.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reason reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon">{{ icons.server }}</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Let us run it, or run it yourself</h3>
          <p>Use the hosted service and never think about infrastructure, or keep data on your own servers with Docker or Kubernetes. The code is the same either way, so switching later is always an option.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reason reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon">{{ icons.scale }}</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Simple, predictable pricing</h3>
          <p>Plans are based on monthly events, not seats. Larger plans include unlimited users and projects, with no surprise overage charges.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reason reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon">{{ icons["sliders-horizontal"] }}</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Change behavior without redeploying</h3>
          <p>Real-time client configuration lets you adjust log levels, ignore noisy errors, and toggle settings in apps that are already running.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reason reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon">{{ icons.code }}</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Deep .NET roots, first-class JavaScript and mobile</h3>
          <p>Born in the .NET world with clients for ASP.NET Core, WPF, console apps, and every major logging library, plus browser and Node.js clients with source map support, and a React Native client that works with Expo.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reason reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon">{{ icons["ai-sparkle"] }}</span>
        <div>
          <h3>AI that works with your data</h3>
          <p>Ask Exie about your errors in plain English, or connect your coding agent through the MCP server. Both use your permissions and only change things when you ask. <a href="/ai/">See how it works</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reason reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon">{{ icons["shield-check"] }}</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Privacy you control</h3>
          <p>Exclude sensitive fields before events leave your app, decide whether to collect private information, and host it all yourself if you need to.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reason reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon">{{ icons["heart-handshake"] }}</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Real people behind it</h3>
          <p>A small, independent team that has been building, running, and supporting Exceptionless for more than a decade.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-sm" aria-label="What developers say">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <figure class="card quote-card reveal">
        <blockquote>"Exceptionless is awesome. I've stopped worrying about whether I'm losing customers to bugs I don't know about."</blockquote>
        <figcaption><strong>Eric B.</strong></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="card quote-card reveal">
        <blockquote>"Exceptionless allows us to prioritize fixes smarter by showing frequently occurring errors. In real time!"</blockquote>
        <figcaption><strong>Ryan H.</strong></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-sm">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="cta reveal">
      <h2>Stop guessing what's broken</h2>
      <p>Set up Exceptionless in minutes and see the errors your users have been quietly running into.</p>
      <div class="btn-group">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="{{ site.signupUrl }}" data-cta="why-footer">Get started {{ icons["arrow-right"] }}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg" href="/tour/">Take the tour</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
